Project Title: World Explorer – Discover Countries and Their Specialities

Project Overview
World Explorer is an interactive web-based experience that allows users to explore different countries and learn about their origins, capitals, and famous landmarks. The website should feel engaging and visually rich, similar to scrolling through an educational travel reel rather than reading a traditional information page. The goal is to make learning about countries fun, simple, and visually appealing through images, animations, and background music.

Concept
The website presents different countries as animated sections. As users scroll through the page, each section introduces a country with its name, capital city, historical origin, and famous landmark images. Each country section should appear with smooth animations so the experience feels like traveling across the world.

Content Structure
Each country section should include:

• Country Name
• National Flag
• Capital City
• Short Origin or Historical Background
• Famous Landmark Images
• Specialities such as food, culture, or natural beauty

Each country must include **1–2 famous images or landmarks** so users can visually connect with the country.

Example Format

Country: Japan
Capital: Tokyo
Origin: Japan has a rich cultural history influenced by samurai traditions and ancient temples.
Famous Images: Mount Fuji, Tokyo city skyline
Specialities: Cherry blossoms, anime culture, sushi.

Country: France
Capital: Paris
Origin: France has played an important role in European history and culture.
Famous Images: Eiffel Tower, Louvre Museum
Specialities: Fashion, art, cuisine.

